From: Daniel Özdek <daniel.timur.23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Give folder-detected Chromium switches only to programs that use Chromium

A program next to libcef.dll/chrome_elf.dll (or icudtl.dat + resources.pak) got
--in-process-gpu --no-sandbox even when it never runs Chromium itself. BeamNG's
CrashRpt CrashSender.exe sits next to the game's CEF copy, rejects the extra
arguments and exits; the game then waits for it forever during crInstall.
The folder markers now only count when the image links libcef/chrome_elf
(directly or delay-loaded), is a .NET image (CefSharp, e.g. Safe Exam Browser)
or exports napi_module_register (Node/Electron). Known browser executable names
and the Electron fuse detection are unchanged.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/env.c
@@ -2025,39 +2025,48 @@
